# 📬 Email System Doctrine: Human Inbox, Gmail Integration, Onboarding, RBAC

This rule defines how the email system works across backend, UI, security, and onboarding. It references concrete files and gives an implementation plan so another agent can extend or complete integrations.

## 1) Components & Current Behavior

- Human Inbox View (server context)
  - File: [crm-deployment/crm/www/human_inbox.py](mdc:crm-deployment/crm/www/human_inbox.py)
  - Purpose: Returns Communications for the Human Inbox page.
  - Scoping: Filters to the logged-in user by:
    - `sender == frappe.session.user` OR `recipients LIKE %user%`
    - If the user owns any Email Accounts, adds `email_account in user-owned accounts` to restrict cross‑user visibility.

- Email Account Provisioning (server API)
  - File: [crm-deployment/crm/api/settings.py](mdc:crm-deployment/crm/api/settings.py)
  - Method: `create_email_account(data)`
  - Creates Frappe `Email Account` with provider presets (Gmail/Outlook/etc.). For non-Frappe-Mail, sets IMAP/SMTP, `enable_incoming`, `enable_outgoing`, and initial sync.

- Draft/Send + Linking Resolver (server API & hooks)
  - File: [crm-deployment/crm/api/email.py](mdc:crm-deployment/crm/api/email.py)
  - Draft/Send helpers already present; resolver/auto-link is added to link Communications to the right Contact/Lead/Org (and optionally prefer open Deal).
  - File: [crm-deployment/crm/hooks.py](mdc:crm-deployment/crm/hooks.py)
    - `doc_events["Communication"]["after_insert"] = "crm.api.email.auto_link_communication"`

- Lead List Permission Guard (server API)
  - File: [crm-deployment/crm/api/doc.py](mdc:crm-deployment/crm/api/doc.py)
  - Adds a default `owner = frappe.session.user` filter for `CRM Lead` when requester is not a manager, preventing cross‑user exposure.

## 2) Email Flow Overview

1) Provision mailbox (per user) → creates `Email Account` owned by that user.
2) Frappe’s Email Receiver pulls IMAP/POP and creates `Communication` docs.
3) Our link resolver ties Communications to Contact/Deal/Lead/Organization (thread → Contact → Deal (opt) → Lead → Org domain).
4) Human Inbox fetches only the current user's Communications (by sender/recipients and owned Email Accounts).
5) Send/Draft uses the user’s own `Email Account` as sender.

## 3) Gmail Integration Options

### A) App Password (Current, works now)
- User opens Human Inbox → “Connect Email” modal → choose Gmail → supply `email_id` and App Password.
- Calls `crm.api.settings.create_email_account` with:
  ```json
  {
    "service": "GMail",
    "email_id": "user@gmail.com",
    "email_account_name": "Gmail - User B",
    "enable_incoming": 1,
    "enable_outgoing": 1,
    "default_incoming": 1,
    "default_outgoing": 1,
    "password": "<app_password>"
  }
  ```
- First sync pulls recent emails; Human Inbox scoping ensures isolation.

### B) OAuth (Near-term improvement)
- Setup Google Cloud project (Gmail/IMAP/SMTP scopes) and whitelist redirect URL.
- Add OAuth endpoints:
  - `crm.api.oauth.start(provider)` → redirect to provider
  - `crm.api.oauth.callback(provider)` → exchange code → store tokens on `Email Account` (custom fields: `oauth_provider`, `access_token`, `refresh_token`, `token_expiry`)
- Update send/receive to use XOAUTH2 where available; keep App Password fallback.

## 4) Human Inbox UI/UX (per-user, self-serve)

- UI entry: `/crm/human_inbox`
- If no accounts found for user → show “Connect Email” CTA.
- Modal options:
  - Provider picker (Gmail/Outlook/etc.)
  - For App Password flow: `email_id`, `password`, flags (incoming/outgoing)
  - For OAuth flow: provider button; complete OAuth, then confirm account settings
- Sending: sender dropdown lists only user-owned accounts; default to primary.

## 5) Security & RBAC

- `Email Account`
  - Ownership: set `owner = frappe.session.user` at creation.
  - Permissions: enable “If Owner” for non-admin roles; managers can see all.

- `Communication`
  - Creation: from puller/receiver with correct `email_account` linkage.
  - Visibility in Human Inbox: scoped by current user (sender/recipients) and `email_account in user-owned` when available.
  - Do not use `ignore_permissions=True` when listing from inbox.

- `CRM Lead`/others
  - Lists default to owner for non-managers (see [crm-deployment/crm/api/doc.py](mdc:crm-deployment/crm/api/doc.py)).

## 6) Implementation Tasks (Another Agent)

1) UI: “Connect Email” modal on Human Inbox page (SPA)
   - Action → `frappe.call("crm.api.settings.create_email_account", data)`
   - After success → toast + refresh inbox; sync runs async.

2) Server: Harden `create_email_account`
   - Validate ownership = current user; ensure `enable_incoming/outgoing` flags.
   - For Gmail: IMAP/SMTP presets, `initial_sync_count` reasonable (e.g., 100), `email_sync_option = ALL`.

3) Server: Confirm link resolver execution
   - Ensure [crm-deployment/crm/hooks.py](mdc:crm-deployment/crm/hooks.py) doc_event is present in production branch.
   - In [crm-deployment/crm/api/email.py](mdc:crm-deployment/crm/api/email.py), verify resolver order: thread → Contact → Deal (if enabled) → Lead → Org domain; optional auto-create Lead behind feature flag.

4) OAuth (optional sprint)
   - Create `crm.api.oauth.start/callback` methods.
   - Add custom fields to `Email Account` for tokens; add secure storage patterns (no Git artifacts).
   - Implement XOAUTH2 auth for Gmail/Outlook; fall back to App Password.

5) Privacy tests
   - Users A/B with separate accounts: A must not see B’s inbox and vice versa.
   - Manager can switch a filter to see multiple, if business rules allow.

## 7) Testing Checklist

- Provision
  - Create Email Account for User B via modal → account saved, ownership = User B.
  - Background sync runs; no errors in logs.

- Inbox Isolation
  - User A sees only A’s sent/received (and A’s accounts).
  - User B sees only B’s.

- Send/Draft
  - Compose with User B → sender is B’s account; draft/store/send succeeds.

- Linking
  - Inbound messages auto-link per resolver; replies inherit reference.

## 8) Acceptance Criteria

- “Connect Email” is self-serve; no admin required for adding a personal mailbox.
- Human Inbox displays only messages for the logged-in user.
- Draft/Send always uses a user-owned `Email Account`.
- Communications get correctly linked to CRM entities by resolver.

